{"agent":"recover-4f","data":{"digest":"5887eddd040d459b","finding":1,"gate":"critic","location":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:141","probe":"Fixed in d05a91587: merge_tree computes one monotonic cutoff (time.monotonic()+deadline_s) and every internal git call (rev-parse, merge-base, merge) takes the time left (timeout=left()), so a slow worktree add cannot buy the merge a second full deadline_s; the total is bounded by the caller's deadline. probe._scratch blocks in-process only for that bounded span.","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:141","verdict":"confirmed"},"id":"e64b25f01463813089116126f","kind":"review.triaged","lamport":155583,"schema":1,"subject":"LK-probe-scratch-deadline","ts":"2026-11-08T15:21:09.714068Z"}
